lesson: 127
title: Stories in two steps
level: primary-1
stars: 1
explain: Some stories change a number twice. Follow the story in order: first one change, then the next.
explain: 25 people were on a bus, 8 got on, then 12 got off: 25 + 8 = 33, then 33 − 12 = 21.
vars: a=name b=name c=name t=thing n=5..50 x=2..30 y=2..40
need: n + x <= 100
need: n + x - y >= 2
answer: n + x - y
exercise: {a} had {n} {t}. {b} gave {a.him} {x} more, and then {a} gave {y} {t} to {c}. How many {t} does {a} have now?
exercise: There were {n} people on a bus. At the first stop {x} got on, and at the second stop {y} got off. How many people are on the bus now?
exercise: {a} had {n} {t}. {a.He} bought {x} more and lost {y}. How many {t} does {a.he} have now?
exercise: A shop had {n} {t}. In the morning {x} more {t} were brought in, and in the afternoon {y} {t} were sold. How many {t} are left in the shop?
exercise: Work out {n} + {x} − {y}.
test: {a} gave away {y} {t} after getting {x} new ones; at the start {a.he} had {n}. How many {t} does {a.he} have at the end?
test: {n} birds sat on a fence. {x} more birds landed on it, and then {y} birds flew away. How many birds are still on the fence?
test: {a} starts the day with {n} marbles. {a.He} wins {x} marbles in a game and gives {y} marbles to {a.his} friends. How many marbles are left at the end of the day?
test: Start at {n}, count on {x}, then count back {y}. Where do you stop?
exercise: {a} had {n} {t}. {b} gave {a.him} another {x}, and then {a} handed {y} to {c}. How many {t} has {a} got now?
exercise: A school bus in Ohio had {n} children on it. {x} got on at the first stop and {y} got off at the second. How many children are on the bus now?
exercise: {a} had {n} {t}, bought {x} more, then lost {y}. How many {t} remain?
exercise: A shop in Belfast had {n} {t}. A delivery brought {x} more, and later {y} were sold. How many {t} does the shop still have?
exercise: What is {n} add {x} take away {y}?
exercise: How many {t} does {a} have at the end, if {a.he} started with {n}, was given {x}, and gave away {y}?
exercise: There were {n} ducks on a pond in Canberra. {x} more ducks flew in, then {y} ducks swam off. How many ducks are on the pond now?
exercise: {c} had {n} {t}. {c.He} got {x} more from {a}, then donated {y} to a charity in Dublin. How many {t} does {c} have left?
test: {a} won {x} marbles and lost {y}; {a.he} began with {n}. How many marbles does {a.he} have now?
test: In a library in Auckland, {n} people were reading. {x} more came in, and then {y} went home. How many people are reading now?
test: A train left Boston with {n} passengers. At the next station {x} people boarded and {y} people got off. How many passengers are on the train after that station?
test: Begin with {n}. Add {x}. Subtract {y}. What is the answer?
test: {b} had {n} {t} in a drawer. {b.His} aunt from Ottawa sent {x} more, and {b} gave {y} to {c}. How many {t} does {b} have now?
test: How many sheep are in the field if there were {n}, the farmer brought {x} more, and {y} were moved to another field?
exercise: had {n} {t}, {b} gave me {x}, i gave {c} {y}. how many now
exercise: bus had {n}, {x+1}, no wait, {x} got on, then {y} got off. how many on now
exercise: {b} added em all: {n+x+y}. {a} had {n} {t}, got {x} more, lost {y}. that's wrong innit? how many {a.he} got
exercise: shop had {n} {t}, {x} more came in the morning (truck was {y+5} mins late), {y} sold in the arvo. how many left
test: {n} birds on the fence, {x} more land, {y} fly off. how many still there
test: {a} started w/ {n} marbles, won {x}, gave {c} {y+2}, no sorry, {y}. how many left
test: start {n}, add {x}, take {y}. {c} reckons {n+x}, forgot the {y}. what's the real answer
exam: It is given that {a} held {n} {t}, subsequently received {x} {t} from {b}, and thereafter transferred {y} {t} to {c}. Determine the number of {t} presently held by {a}.
exam: Whereas a bus conveyed {n} passengers, whereupon a further {x} passengers boarded at the first stop and {y} passengers alighted at the second stop, ascertain the number of passengers presently aboard.
exam: {a}, initially in possession of {n} {t}, acquired a further {x} {t} and subsequently mislaid {y} {t}. State the number of {t} remaining.
exam: Compute the result of increasing {n} by {x} and thereafter diminishing the sum by {y}.
exercise: There were {n} people on the coach to Grandad's funeral. {x} more got on in town, and {y} got off at the church. How many people were still on the coach?
exercise: A factory had {n} workers. It took on {x} more in spring, but in autumn {y} were "made redundant". How many workers does it have now?
test: had {n} {t}. nan gave me {x}, then {c} "borrowed" {y}, never coming back are they. how many i got
